# Compose environment for the NAS deployment (copied to $NAS_STACK_DIR/.env by `make deploy-nas`).
# No secrets here: the API key and Kalshi key files are mounted from ./secrets on the NAS.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://harness:harness@postgres:5432/harness
ODDS_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/odds_api_key
ODDS_API_BOOKMAKERS=pinnacle,betonlineag,lowvig,draftkings,fanduel,novig,kalshi
TZ=UTC
# Run the app containers as the NAS user so the 0600 secret files are readable without chown/sudo.
APP_UID=1000
APP_GID=10
# Host port for the health/dashboard endpoint (8080 is taken by SABnzbd on the NAS).
SERVE_PORT=8180
# Paper posture, asserted positively. Absence of a live-trading flag proves nothing to a later
# reader; a committed 0 in every revision of this file is a provable statement that the deployed
# harness places no real orders. See docs/legal-posture.md. Flipping either value is a gate.
LIVE_TRADING=0
HARNESS_MODE=paper
# Informational only: writes stay dormant regardless (Settings.kalshi_env already defaults to
# this). Committed so the posture file -- the artifact a later reader audits -- states it too.
KALSHI_ENV=prod
# U5 (Task 4b step 5): the gate row is judged on sharp_two_sided from the phase 3 deploy on
GATE_VARIANT=sharp_two_sided
# Phase 4.5 snapshot scheduler, off since 2026-09-10 04:37Z: its builders' reads starved the
# executor (journal 89-90). Fix 31 bounds every builder read, halves the cadences, caps Study
# per tick and adds a self-guard. Flip this to 1 only after fix 31's `Scheduler re-enable`
# row in verify.md has passed on a real 15-minute window, and set it back on any failure.
# On its own line, like every other comment here: `docker run --env-file` does not strip a
# trailing comment, so an inline one would deploy the value `0  # ...`.
SNAPSHOTS_ENABLED=1
# Phase 5 (addendum §1.4, ruling B-M14). The research worker in app-research: the shadow veto
# and the weekly report annotator. Set to 0 to stop both without touching the container; the
# worker still starts and idles. Separate from the key: without secrets/anthropic_api_key the
# worker is dormant whatever this says, and reports "research: dormant, no key".
# On its own line, like every other comment here: `docker run --env-file` does not strip a
# trailing comment, so an inline one would deploy the value `1  # ...`.
RESEARCH_WORKER_ENABLED=1
# Phase 5 (addendum §1.6, ruling B-M3). The combo RFQ listener's second WebSocket connection
# inside app-ws. Set to 0 to stop it; the market tape is unaffected either way, because the
# listener owns its own connection and its own reconnect.
RFQ_LISTENER_ENABLED=1
